<article class="env-lemma" id="0ERB">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0ERB">Lemma <span data-tag="0ERB">82.23.3</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/0EDT" data-tag="0EDT">82.2.1</a> let $X/B$ be good. Let $(\mathcal{L}, s, i : D \to X)$ be a triple as in Definition <a href="/tag/0ER1" data-tag="0ER1">82.22.1</a>. Let $\mathcal{N}$ be an invertible $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module. Then $i^*(c_1(\mathcal{N}) \cap \alpha ) = c_1(i^*\mathcal{N}) \cap i^*\alpha $ in $\mathop{\mathrm{CH}}\nolimits _{k - 2}(D)$ for all $\alpha \in \mathop{\mathrm{CH}}\nolimits _ k(Z)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      With exactly the same proof as in Lemma <a href="/tag/0ERA" data-tag="0ERA">82.23.2</a> this follows from Lemmas <a href="/tag/0EQT" data-tag="0EQT">82.19.4</a>, <a href="/tag/0EQZ" data-tag="0EQZ">82.21.3</a>, and <a href="/tag/0ER9" data-tag="0ER9">82.23.1</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>